Welcome to Part 2 =E2=9C=8C=EF=B8=8F=F0=9F=98=B2=E2=9C=8C=EF=B8=8F

Tuesday
Today was an awesome DCM in person! We actually did make it to Tottori, and
we learned a lot as well! We all met together afterwards to eat Udon (and
the desert we brought all the way to Yonago). The rest of our day was
unfortunately traveling back home lol. The trains do not like us.

Wednesday
Today we visited Ogi San again, and brought him some fruit! He was super
reluctant to take any but in the end agreed to take one. Later we will
visit him again! We tried some housing on the way back to the church, to
little avail. No reason to be discouraged though! I believe that we are
leaving an impact on even the people that initially refuse us. Today we
also met up and got some ramen for dinner with Mitani Kyoudai!! Great day!

Thursday
Today was SKK so we didn't do much besides planning. It was pretty
productive as far as planning goes, so that's great! We also had the lesson
with Mitani Kyoudai at the church, and afterwards Japanese class at the
community center. I swear I need to start tape recording these
conversations. I swear the mix of personalities between us at that table in
the community center is crazy. Fujita Sensei referenced =E2=80=9CLets Make =
a Deal=E2=80=9D
and we had to guess which of 3 boxes a toy car was inside of. It was
insanely deep psychological stuff and I felt my brain like grow 3 sizes
even if I can=E2=80=99t explain anything that I learned that night. Next ti=
me I'm
gonna bring Uno and we are gonna play it at our table lol. I=E2=80=99m look=
ing
forward to it!!

Dreamed about =E3=81=95=E3=81=8F=E3=81=A1=E3=82=93, Bananas, an arcade (may=
be?) =E6=9B=B8=E5=BA=97=E4=BC=9A

Friday
Today we did some sign streeting in front of a high school! Well, we
started off by doing sign streeting. The approach that Nakazawa=E9=95=B7=E8=
=80=81 wanted to
use was to try drawing pokemon for students, then invite them to our
Eikawa. We ended talking with a handful of students but only 3 took a
request for the drawing. The first person was a girl who we've talked with
a couple times randomly at this point. She's very quiet and composed, and
even though we didn't talk with her about the gospel this time around, I
really feel like she would listen and have an interest in it if we are
genuine with her. After our finding at the high school, we headed back to
the church for game night. I dominated uno as usual, and played some super
fun ping pong with Matsuoka San. We shared a couple scriptures for our
spiritual thought, here they are:
Alma 37:6-7
6 Now ye may suppose that this is foolishness in me; but behold I say unto
you, that by small and simple things are great things brought to pass; and
small means in many instances doth confound the wise. 7 And the Lord God
doth work by means to bring about his great and eternal purposes; and by
very small means the Lord doth confound the wise and bringeth about the
salvation of many souls.
These are pretty famous scriptures in our church, but that's no reason to
downplay their importance and truth. If we spend our time looking for big
miracles and =E2=80=9Cmeaningful=E2=80=9D things, we are going to lose sigh=
t of the
countless simple wonders and tender mercies that are abundant in our lives.
Look for the details. Look for God's love. I promise that you will find it.

Saturday
My dreams were actually insane tonight. Dreamed about:
Kanye, birds turning into burgers that when placed on my head communicated
with me, pizza, fishing watches out of sand with my companion, weird stuff

Chivalry is not dead!
Today we studied the Book of Mormon with members, and helped give some
water to an almost dead cat at the church. We were also able to do some
housing and gave out a decent amount of Eikaiwa flyers. There were
definitely a few people we met with good potential! Pray that they will
follow through on what they felt and call us =F0=9F=98=81Earlier today we w=
ere able
to meet with Katayama san and talk a bit about his thoughts on religion. I
can tell that there's a change working in his heart. We were able to join a
small concert that he invited us to, and it was pretty neat. There were 3
ladies performing songs from Gibli movies, and before the performance I
noticed they were struggling to set up one of their phones against a box to
record their performance. So, with my nice fancy phone stand, I strolled
over and offered It to them to use. They were super happy!! At amother
point today I also got the door for a lady wheeling product into a Combini;
Chivalry isn't dead. =F0=9F=98=8E=F0=9F=98=8E

Sunday
Long long long long long
Today we were at the church from 9AM until 5PM. It was all pretty
productive, but definitely took a loooong time. We were so hungry by the
end =F0=9F=98=85

=F0=9F=8C=9FSome more poetry? Don't mind me-=F0=9F=8C=9F

Trains trains trains trains trains
Trains trains trains trains trains trains trains
Trains trains trains trains trains

This could be just a personal problem
But writing the same word time after time
I begin to question the truth in the spelling
And the spelling certainly questions mine

I need to go to the bathroom
I haven't since I left the church
And I fear I face doom
When I feel my stomach lurch

My companion was asked to order me some water
From the vending machine.
However, I felt the urge to slaughter
When a different drink he handed me
(An exaggeration by the way lol)

A face in the fog in my mind
I don't know whose it may be
Honestly, I don't mind
As long as I can see
A face in the fog in my mind
I don't know whose it may be
Honestly, I don't mind
As long as I can see
That there's a reason to move past the trials and grief that at times we
experience
It's not going to last forever, I trust
I'm willing to bet more than a pence
That it'll be for my good, therefore my hardships are a must
A face in the fog smiles back

=E8=8A=B1=E3=81=8C=E5=92=B2=E3=81=8F
=E3=81=A7=E3=81=AF=E3=81=AA=E3=81=84=E3=83=BC=E7=AC=91
=E6=9A=91=E3=81=99=E3=81=8E=E3=81=A0

=E7=A7=8B=E6=9D=A5=E3=82=93=E3=81=AD
=E6=97=A5=E3=81=8C=E7=B5=82=E3=82=8F=E3=82=93=E3=81=AD=E3=83=BC
=E3=81=AD=E3=81=87=E3=83=BC =E3=81=AA=E3=81=9C=EF=BC=9F

=E3=82=A6=E3=82=BD=E3=81=A3=E3=81=BD=E3=81=84
=E5=83=95=E3=81=AE=E8=A9=A9=E3=81=8C =E3=81=A1
=E3=82=87=E3=81=A3=E3=81=A8=E5=A4=89

Pday
Today has been crazy already. We started off the day by calling our
families at the church, then started biking to a pretty far away Mcdonalds
to meet up with a girl named Yuzuki. On the way we stopped by the trusty
card shop and got some beyond reasonably discounted cards, then biked like
30-40 minutes in the heat. It was a pretty fun bike ride, and we got to see
a few places I've never been to before in Tsuyama along the way. We got
there a decent bit earlier than expected, so we ordered a drink and waited
for Yuzuki to show up. Yuzuki showed up, we ate and talked for a little
while, and explained to her a bit about the word of wisdom. She was pretty
surprised that we don't drink tea or coffee! She said she works at
Starbucks and I told her about how Sakurako from Sennan works at a caf=C3=
=A9 and
is planning on getting baptized this year =F0=9F=98=B2 They are only a year=
 apart
from each other, so hopefully Yuzuki San can consider joining our church as
something that is a possibility for her. After Mcdonalds, we biked over to
the shopping mall and took some photos at a photo booth, and walked around
the dollar store before realizing we had to leave right then or we wouldn't
be able to take our train! So, we said goodbye and rushed to the station=E2=
=80=A6
we just barely made it. On the way Nakazawa=E9=95=B7=E8=80=81=E2=80=99s bac=
k tire Popped, and a
lady almost ran me over. We are gonna have to worry about the bike when we
get back, but somehow even with the flat we were able to make it to the
station in the nick of time. After that, it was just trains until we made
it to Yonago. At least I hope we made it! Guess We will find out next week
=E2=9C=8C=EF=B8=8F

Well, congrats! You've made it to the end of my email. I love you so much!!

Let's do our best this next week!

Love, Elder Killian

